X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260916T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260916T180000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Cite It Right with NoodleTools: MLA APA @ 5PM on Sept 16 (via Zoom)
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliog
 raphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features
 \, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Deta
 ils: Extra Credit available!This NoodleTools workshop will focus on the M
 LA APA citation styles.Check with your instructor to confirm the citation
  style appropriate for your research assignment.When writing a research p
 aper\, the discipline typically determines the citation style you will us
 e.In this workshop\, you will learn how to sign up for an account with No
 odleTools. We will also provide examples to show how to create citations\
 , create a bibliography and check for errors. There will be time to ask q
 uestions at the end of the overview —bring your sources along. Join us 
 and learn how to cite your sources right!Extra Credit: As students\, you 
 have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you regist
 er if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attended 
 the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on 
 an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.Registration: (
 click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requires registrati
 on in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a confirm
 ation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam fol
 der if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to
  allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student co
 nduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to 
 join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA cita
 tions and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper
 -writing features\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleD
 ocs.<br />Workshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools
  workshop will focus on the MLA APA citation styles.<br />Check with your
  instructor to confirm the citation style appropriate for your research a
 ssignment.<br />When writing a research paper\, the discipline typically 
 determines the citation style you will use.<br />In this workshop\, you w
 ill learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will also pr
 ovide examples to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography an
 d check for errors. There will be time to ask questions at the end of the
  overview —bring your sources along. Join us and learn how to cite your
  sources right!<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to s
 ubmit your instructor and course name when you register if you would like
  us to notify your instructor that you have attended the workshop for ext
 ra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative way t
 o provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Registration: (click "Begin R
 egistration" button below)<br />This workshop requires registration in or
 der to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will receive a confirmat
 ion email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam folde
 r if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes earl
 y to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC 
 student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute 
 video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SR
 JC Librarian!
