X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T180000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Top 10 Research Hacks You Need to Know (via Zoom)
DESCRIPTION:Interested in some "wow-I-wish-I-had-known-that!" research ti
 ps for your next project or paper? Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris as 
 she shares her top 10 research hacks…based on feedback from faculty\, s
 taff\, and most important\, students!This 30-minute session will include 
 an opportunity to ask questions an option to stay longer and learn how to
  use the A.I. Research Assistant in SRJC Libraries' Smart Search.Extra Cr
 edit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and cou
 rse name when you register if your instructor is offering extra credit an
 d you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attended. Or\
 , you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide evid
 ence of your attendance.Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button 
 below)Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This worksho
 p requires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You w
 ill receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop
 . Check your spam folder if you don't see it.This Zoom workshop will open
  10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abid
 e by SRJC student conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-min
 ute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC
  Librarian!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Interested in some "wow-I-wish-I-had-known-t
 hat!" research tips for your next project or paper? Join SRJC Librarian J
 essica Harris as she shares her top 10 research hacks…based on feedback
  from faculty\, staff\, and most important\, students!<br />This 30-minut
 e session will include an opportunity to ask questions an option to stay 
 longer and learn how to use the A.I. Research Assistant in SRJC Libraries
 ' Smart Search.<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to s
 ubmit your instructor and course name when you register if your instructo
 r is offering extra credit and you would like us to notify your instructo
 r that you have attended. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an al
 ternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Registration: 
 (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />Registration: (click "Begi
 n Registration" button below)<br />This workshop requires registration in
  order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will receive a confir
 mation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam fo
 lder if you don't see it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes ea
 rly to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJ
 C student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minut
 e video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Chat with an 
 SRJC Librarian!
