LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research Cite It Right with NoodleTools @ 5p
 m\, Sept 21 via Zoom
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris and learn how to simplify 
 citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score qui
 ck tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.Noodle
 Tools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offe
 rs note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the c
 apability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit 
 available!This NoodleTools workshop will use the MLA citation style\, whi
 ch is typically used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and
  Religion disciplines.If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will 
 share how to choose this option in NoodleTools too.You will learn how to 
 sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show
  how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.Alo
 ng the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible research
  in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to confirm the 
 citation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extra Credit: As 
 students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name 
 when you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you
  have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your
  instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.
 Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requ
 ires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will re
 ceive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Chec
 k your spam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 m
 inutes early to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by 
 SRJC student conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute v
 ideo on how to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Libr
 arian!Image credit: Gaelen Pinnock\, CC BY-SA 4.0 \, via Wikimedia Common
 s
