LOCATION:Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:Artist Walk-Through - Tom Chown: 46 Years Behind the Lens
DESCRIPTION:Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24\, working in the cam
 pus photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he became a familiar presen
 ce throughout the college community\, documenting the people\, programs a
 nd milestones that shaped generations of students and employees.  The exh
 ibition will trace Chown's evolution as a photographer\, from working wit
 h film and developing photographs in the darkroom to embracing digital ph
 otography. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments f
 rom nearly five decades of college life.  The exhibition will trace Chown
 's evolution as a photographer\, from working with film and developing ph
 otographs in the darkroom to embracing digital photography. It also offer
 s a visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments from nearly five decades 
 of college life.  The exhibition is free and open to the public.Location:
  Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Doyle Library 1st floor - Santa Rosa Cam
 pusFor more information\, visit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery webs
 ite. (https://art-gallery.santarosa.edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-wor
 k)
