BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T120000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Neha Saigal - Human Agency & Machine Inquiry
DESCRIPTION:As generative AI becomes embedded across disciplines\, higher
  education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle between opposing camps\
 , but of intentional design.  Generative systems offer novel capabilities
  for research\, creation\, and learning\, yet their ultimate value depend
 s entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.Neha Saigal is building AI-n
 ative learning tools grounded in how kids are actually wired to learn.Lea
 rn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website. (https://cs.santa
 rosa.edu/ai-talks-2026)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As generative AI becomes embedded acros
 s disciplines\, higher education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle b
 etween opposing camps\, but of intentional design.</p><p>  Generative sys
 tems offer novel capabilities for research\, creation\, and learning\, ye
 t their ultimate value depends entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them
 .</p><p><strong>Neha Saigal</strong> is building AI-native learning tools
  grounded in how kids are actually wired to learn.</p><p><a href="https:/
 /cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn mor
 e on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website.</a></p>
UID:20261120T190000Z-23947@calendar.santarosa.edu
