BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270304
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:Standing in Her Power: Portraits Beyond the Colonial Frame
DESCRIPTION:In early May 2026\, we put out a call for nominations\, askin
 g for Native American women to represent their Nations\, their stories\, 
 and their strength through a powerful portrait exhibition celebrating ide
 ntity\, cultural legacy\, and the resilience of Native women. Every singl
 e entry showed us how beautiful and unique and strong Native American wom
 en are.  Two days of photo sessions were held in the Museum in August wit
 h photographer Alexa Treviňo of LexMex Art.This Exhibit is funded by a g
 rant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultur
 al Enrichment Endowment.For more information\, visit the SRJC Multicultur
 al Museum website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power
 -portraits-beyond-colonial-frame)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In early May 2026\, we put out a call f
 or nominations\, asking for Native American women to represent their Nati
 ons\, their stories\, and their strength through a powerful portrait exhi
 bition celebrating identity\, cultural legacy\, and the resilience of Nat
 ive women. Every single entry showed us how beautiful and unique and stro
 ng Native American women are.</p><p>  Two days of photo sessions were hel
 d in the Museum in August with photographer Alexa Treviňo of LexMex Art.
 </p><p><em>This Exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior C
 ollege Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.</em></p>
 <p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portrai
 ts-beyond-colonial-frame" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more informa
 tion\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museum website.</a></p>
